  annotation "note_1771590377139_1", anchor: "the failed expansions are not commemorated", text: "The ice commemorates them. Three distinct retreat-signatures at stratum 4 near the Promenade Ward. Two correspond to periods the official timeline calls 'consolidation pauses.' The third matches nothing in any chronicle. Someone was lost there and no one wrote it down.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590377139_2", anchor: "Whether it survives a governance model that requires clear skies during a period of increasing darkness", text: "My annotation on the Clear-sky Mandate describes the trap: a clear-sky requirement for all votes includes the vote to repeal it. Under clouds, no reform is possible. Under clear skies, no reform feels necessary. I called it elegant. Now, watching it close on a faction that cannot convene its own succession — with the Long Dark approaching and fire-core rationing at Third Tier — elegant is not the word I would choose.", type: :commentary, display: :full
